        "subject": "LU-21072 build: Use build when source is unusable",
        "message": "LU-21072 build: Use build when source is unusable\n\nSince Linux 6.6 (d8131c2965d5) /lib/modules/<ver>/source is no\nlonger created, so the lustre-client DKMS build fails to find\nthe kernel source.\n\nUse build when source is missing or has no include/linux, as\ndkms.mkconf does. Also do this for the kdir default in\nlustre.spec.in.\n\nFixes: 0142d86fda55 (\"LU-17233 dkms: support for kfilnd and gnilnd\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Xiao Yang <xyang@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: I14b2e9657e79506c0a1f6ed2bc218982d2b1d562\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70216\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Alex Zhuravlev <azhuravlev@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Jian Yu <yujian@nvidia.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
